retro_run stops when the game has ended

retro_run ran System::RunLoop until a frame was submitted. Two statuses never
submit one: ShutdownRequested (the game closed itself, or a reset during its
initial setup) and ErrorNotInitialized, which every later RunLoop returns once
an in-game reboot (APT/NS RequestReset, System::Reset = Shutdown then Load)
could not load the title again. The loop then never returned: it posted a
message on every pass, and the frontend's lock around retro_run was held for
good, so its next pause or save waited forever (audit, 2026-10-20).

On any status but Success the loop now reports it as before, tells the
frontend the game has ended (RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_SHUTDOWN, LibRetro::Shutdown)
and returns. In the libretro build no other status reaches it: save and load
go through retro_serialize, not RunLoop's signals, and ErrorSystemFiles is
returned by Load, not by RunLoop.

--- a/src/citra_libretro/citra_libretro.cpp
+++ b/src/citra_libretro/citra_libretro.cpp
@@ -305,6 +305,13 @@
             }
 
             LibRetro::DisplayMessage(msg.c_str());
+            // No status but Success ever submits a frame here: the game closed
+            // itself (ShutdownRequested), or an in-game reboot left the system
+            // off (ErrorNotInitialized at every later call). Looping on it
+            // never returned, with the frontend's core lock held; the
+            // frontend is told the game has ended instead.
+            LibRetro::Shutdown();
+            return;
         }
     }
 }
